{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3458","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3458","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3458\",\"parent_revision\":\"c164ada62acf6c703e191fbfeaf3f440a212be6c8dec3ebf1acd07505bd06396\",\"root_revision\":\"c164ada62acf6c703e191fbfeaf3f440a212be6c8dec3ebf1acd07505bd06396\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`_update_item_description` (`backlog_core/operations.py:727`) writes the item record and returns. `_rename_item_title` (`:692`), grooming, and striking each perform an immediate targeted reconcile after their write. Description alone does not.\\n\\nThe update is not lost \u2014 it reaches the backend through `put_work_item` \u2192 `_cache._queue_work_item` (`github_work_items.py:459`), and `description` is part of `synchronized_fingerprint` (`reconciliation.py:90`). It arrives on the next reconcile, at unbounded delay.\\n\\n## What that produces\\n\\nA caller that updates a description and then reads the item back through any path that consults the backend sees the previous value, for an interval nothing bounds or reports. A caller that updates a title in the same operation sees that change immediately, so the two halves of one edit become visible at different times.\\n\\n## Two docstrings state the opposite of the code\\n\\n- `backlog_core/server.py:2616` \u2014 the `backlog_update` `description` parameter reads \\\"Updates the local file only \u2014 no GitHub sync.\\\"\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py:728` \u2014 \\\"Update the backend-owned item description. Provider-only, no GitHub sync.\\\"\\n\\nBoth describe a behaviour the code does not have. Acting on them means concluding the tool cannot update a description at all and reaching for a direct `gh issue edit` instead \u2014 which is the path that triggers #3457.\\n\\n## Correction to a plausible reading\\n\\nThere is no separate representation for a description as distinct from groomed sections: both render into one body and one patch. Groom-after-description is therefore safe \u2014 both mutations sit on the same record and one reconcile carries both. An earlier reading of this item held that the correct target representation was an open design question; it is not, and `ARCHITECTURE.md:835` already settles the related rule about which body the sync path may write.\\n\\n## Scope note\\n\\nBelongs with #3457. The two are one commit and two bugs: this one is a missing reconcile trigger plus two wrong docstrings; that one is silent data loss on a different path.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session audit of backlog_core write paths, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope Note\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nBelongs with #3457. The two are one commit and two bugs: this one is a missing reconcile trigger plus two wrong docstrings; that one is silent data loss on a different path.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Correction To A Plausible Reading\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThere is no separate representation for a description as distinct from groomed sections: both render into one body and one patch. Groom-after-description is therefore safe \u2014 both mutations sit on the same record and one reconcile carries both. An earlier reading of this item held that the correct target representation was an open design question; it is not, and `ARCHITECTURE.md:835` already settles the related rule about which body the sync path may write.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What That Produces\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA caller that updates a description and then reads the item back through any path that consults the backend sees the previous value, for an interval nothing bounds or reports. A caller that updates a title in the same operation sees that change immediately, so the two halves of one edit become visible at different times.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Two Docstrings State The Opposite Of The Code\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `backlog_core/server.py:2616` \u2014 the `backlog_update` `description` parameter reads \\\"Updates the local file only \u2014 no GitHub sync.\\\"\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py:728` \u2014 \\\"Update the backend-owned item description. Provider-only, no GitHub sync.\\\"\\n\\nBoth describe a behaviour the code does not have. Acting on them means concluding the tool cannot update a description at all and reaching for a direct `gh issue edit` instead \u2014 which is the path that triggers #3457.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"8fc3ecb3d18ec955edfd15f7e9d1a3ec93562b159e3af66a42157175fd72295e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSAI-A\"}"}